  "gate": {
    "blocks_renting_on_conditioning_grounds": false,
    "verdict": "Worst-cell conditioning degrades about 1.4x per level and the preflight cannot see it -- it records folds, not conditioning -- so it is worth recording. It does NOT block the batch: gci_M, gci_F, gci_FF are worse conditioned than the reference mesh, and that reference mesh converged to its stopping rule and is gate-ACCEPTED. What blocks the batch is the wall-normal divergence (reports/s8_normal_direction.json), which is a different finding entirely.",
    "cheap_test_available": "gci_C_normal_s0_b is 788k cells, fits this host, and stalls under ANK-only, so 'can the solver handle a mesh like gci_F' can be probed here rather than rented. NKSwitchTol matters: the governed 1e-6 never fires, because the stall begins at a relative residual of 1.7e-4, 170x above it."
  }
